Z||000000||JeffreyP21||12-07-2001||04:38 PM||||Hey, i just bought new kenwood 4x10's for the dash..bought a pioneer reciever and am planning on buying a kicker subwoofer..now for more speakers. what speakers fit and where should i place them? whats a good kind to purchase also? please help me out..<BR> Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-07-2001||09:47 PM||||Click on this link:<P>Many useful idea's.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016121.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/016121.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||12-08-2001||12:51 AM||||If you have a car w/ headrest speaers I'd put a good pair 3 1/2's in each seat. Eclipse, Image Dynamics, MB Quart or Focal I think that this sounds the best with a sub. or 4X6's go in the B pillar (the stock location if you don't have headrest speakers) the head rest speakers will yeld better imageing (like head phones) that the 4X6's (like off center book shelf speakers)<P>     I you are planing on a sub like the Kicker Comp VR or XPL <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>  makes a decent .5 cu ft box that replaces the center console and holds a 10" sub (XPL should fit nice) and <A HREF="http://www.subbox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.subbox.com</A>  makes a good looking 12" bandpass box for the spare tire area this one needs a hole cut in the floor board for a port into the cabin. this one would yeld more soun pressure at the cost of sound quality while a top notch sub (Eclipse 8810 or Focal Polly Kevlar/Glass) would sound alot cleaner than a similar sub up front. however you could also get away with less of a sub up front (lower quality) and not notice much loss due the the bandpss box.<P>------------------<BR>  <BR>Black 88 Coupe: 120 MPH spedo, Aux. gauge pod, 195/55VR14 Potenza RE-71 tires, GT exhaust & ground F/X Soon to have 16" White Beretta GTZ W/ 215/45ZR16's<BR><A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A>||||reg||1
